🧠 Research System Architecture (RSA)

Enterprise Multi-Agent Research and Report Generation Framework

📌 Overview

The Research System Architecture (RSA) is a multi-agent system designed to transform user questions into structured, high-quality research reports.

The system:

Accepts user questions

Clarifies ambiguity when required

Conducts deep research using tools

Aggregates and compresses findings

Produces a final report

This architecture follows a modular design where specialized agents collaborate to execute research efficiently.

🎯 Problem Statement

Users often ask broad or unclear questions that require:

Clarification

Structured planning

Multi-source research

Data aggregation

Clear reporting

RSA addresses this by orchestrating multiple agents that perform focused responsibilities.

🧩 Component Responsibilities
Component	Responsibility
Scoping Agent	Clarifies question & prepares research brief
Researcher Agent	Conducts research using tools
Supervisor Agent	Coordinates research strategy
Report Generator	Produces final report
🏗️ High-Level Architecture

The system uses a layered agent-based workflow:

Scoping Layer — defines research scope

Orchestration Layer — supervises execution

Research Layer — performs tool-based research

Processing Layer — compresses findings

Output Layer — generates final report

🔄 End-to-End Research Flow
Diagram
flowchart TB

    User[User Question] --> Scope[Scoping Agent]
    Scope --> Brief[Research Brief]

    Brief --> Supervisor[Supervisor Agent]

    Supervisor --> Researcher[Researcher Agents]
    Researcher --> Tools[Research Tools]
    Tools --> Compress[Compress Findings]

    Compress --> Aggregate[Aggregate Results]
    Aggregate --> Report[Final Report Generation]

    Report --> Output[Final Report]

🔁 Sequence Diagram (Execution Flow)
Diagram
sequenceDiagram

    participant User
    participant Scope as Scoping Agent
    participant Supervisor
    participant Researcher as Researcher Agents
    participant Tools as Research Tools
    participant Compress as Compression Unit
    participant Report as Report Generator

    User->>Scope: Submit Question
    Scope->>User: Clarification (if required)
    Scope->>Supervisor: Send Research Brief

    Supervisor->>Researcher: Assign Research Tasks
    Researcher->>Tools: Execute Tool Calls
    Tools-->>Researcher: Return Research Data

    Researcher->>Compress: Send Raw Findings
    Compress-->>Supervisor: Compressed Results

    Supervisor->>Report: Aggregated Research
    Report-->>User: Final Report

⚙️ System Workflow
1️⃣ Scoping Phase

Clarifies user intent

Defines research boundaries

Produces structured research brief

2️⃣ Planning & Orchestration

Supervisor analyzes research brief

Determines required research tasks

Assigns work to researchers

3️⃣ Research Execution

Researchers invoke tools

Collect data from multiple sources

Summarize outputs

4️⃣ Compression & Aggregation

Findings compressed to reduce noise

Supervisor merges outputs

5️⃣ Report Generation

Final report assembled

Delivered to user

🧱 Design Principles

Separation of concerns between agents

Tool abstraction for extensibility

Scalable orchestration model

Structured reasoning flow

Reusable architecture

📈 Scalability

The architecture supports:

Parallel researcher execution

Multi-tool research workflows

Horizontal scaling via additional agents

Flexible orchestration strategies

🛡️ Reliability & Failure Handling

Possible issues:

Tool failures

Incomplete research

Ambiguous user queries

Mitigation strategies:

Clarification loops

Supervisor re-planning

Result compression and validation

Partial-result fallback

🚀 Future Enhancements

Parallel researcher swarms

Quality scoring pipeline

Automated source validation

Confidence scoring

Multi-stage reasoning graphs

Observability & monitoring

📄 Summary

RSA is an enterprise-grade architecture designed for:

Deep research workflows

Agent orchestration systems

Automated report generation

AI-driven knowledge platforms
